Relevant columns and their potential usage  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES  
  – "geometry": actual polygon/line/point; will be converted to GEOGRAPHY for spatial tests.  
  – "all_tags": contains key/value pairs; needed to locate the multipolygon with {key:'wikidata', value:'Q1095'}.  
  – "feature_type": helps restrict search to multipolygons.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS  
  – "geometry": GEOGRAPHY for every relation; used to test whether it overlaps the area of the Q1095 feature.  
  – "all_tags": used to be sure every candidate relation has a name but no wikidata tag.  
  – "members": list of feature ids belonging to the relation; later joined to PLANET_FEATURES so we can inspect member tags.  
  – "id": primary‑key for every relation.  

• GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES  (again)  
  – used a second time when we join a relation’s “members” with the individual features in order to check if at least one member carries a wikidata tag.  

Conditions that will be useful  

1. In PLANET_FEATURES, filter WHERE f.value:"key" = 'wikidata' AND f.value:"value" = 'Q1095'.  
2. Convert “geometry” to GEOGRAPHY with TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry").  
3. In PLANET_RELATIONS, make sure relation has a name tag (key = 'name') AND does NOT have a wikidata tag.  
4. ST_INTERSECTS( rel_geog , q1095_geog ) OR ST_DWITHIN( … , … , 0 ) to ensure spatial overlap.  
5. Use LATERAL FLATTEN to explode “members” and “all_tags”.  
6. GROUP BY relation id to count number of distinct members; ORDER BY that count DESC to find the one with the most.  

-----------------------------------------------------------------
Ten exploratory / incremental Snowflake SQL queries (each limited to 20 rows)  

```sql
-- 1.  Quickly list any multipolygons that carry the wikidata tag Q1095
SELECT DISTINCT f."feature_type",
       f."osm_way_id",
       t.value:"key"::STRING  AS tag_key,
       t.value:"value"::STRING AS tag_val
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
WHERE  t.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
  AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2.  Retrieve the geometry (as GEOGRAPHY) of the Q1095 multipolygon
SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY(f."geometry")      AS q1095_geog,
       f."osm_way_id",
       f."feature_type"
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
WHERE  t.value:"key"  = 'wikidata'
  AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
  AND  f."feature_type" = 'multipolygons'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3.  Inspect what a relation's tags look like (sample 20)
SELECT r."id",
       r."username",
       t.value:"key"::STRING  AS tag_key,
       t.value:"value"::STRING AS tag_val
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") t
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4.  Find relations that have a name tag but no wikidata tag
SELECT DISTINCT r."id",
       name_t.value:"value"::STRING AS rel_name
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") name_t
WHERE  name_t.value:"key" = 'name'
  AND  NOT EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
        WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
      )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5.  Preview how relation members are stored
SELECT r."id",
       m.value::VARCHAR AS raw_member
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6.  Count members for relations that have a name but no wikidata tag
SELECT r."id",
       COUNT(*) AS member_cnt
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
WHERE  EXISTS (SELECT 1
               FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") nt
               WHERE  nt.value:"key" = 'name')
  AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                   FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
                   WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata')
GROUP  BY r."id"
ORDER  BY member_cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7.  Intersect those candidate relations with the Q1095 multipolygon
WITH q1095 AS (
     SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
     WHERE  t.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
       AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
     LIMIT 1
)
SELECT r."id",
       name_t.value:"value"::STRING AS rel_name
FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
       q1095,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") name_t
WHERE  name_t.value:"key" = 'name'
  AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                   FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
                   WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata')
  AND  ST_INTERSECTS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q1095.g )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8.  Check if at least one member feature of those relations has a wikidata tag
WITH q1095 AS (
     SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
     WHERE  t.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
       AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
     LIMIT 1
),
candidate_rel AS (
     SELECT r."id" AS rel_id,
            r."geometry" AS rel_geom
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
            q1095
     WHERE  ST_INTERSECTS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q1095.g )
       AND  EXISTS (SELECT 1
                    FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") nt
                    WHERE  nt.value:"key" = 'name')
       AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
                        WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata')
)
SELECT cr.rel_id,
       COUNT(*)            AS member_with_wikidata
FROM   candidate_rel       cr
JOIN   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r
       ON r."id" = cr.rel_id,
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
JOIN   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f
       ON f."osm_way_id"::VARCHAR = m.value::STRING,    -- member may be way; adjust if node/rel
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
WHERE  t.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
GROUP  BY cr.rel_id
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9.  Combine everything and rank relations by total members inside the Q1095 area
WITH q1095 AS (
     SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
     WHERE  t.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
       AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
     LIMIT 1
),
candidate_rel AS (
     SELECT r."id",
            name_t.value:"value"::STRING AS rel_name
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
            q1095,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") name_t
     WHERE  name_t.value:"key" = 'name'
       AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
                        WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata')
       AND  ST_INTERSECTS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q1095.g )
)
SELECT c.rel_name,
       c.id                       AS relation_id,
       COUNT(*)                   AS total_members,
       SUM( CASE WHEN wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata' THEN 1 ELSE 0 END )
                                   AS members_with_wikidata
FROM   candidate_rel c
JOIN   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r
       ON r."id" = c."id",
       LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
LEFT JOIN GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f
       ON f."osm_way_id"::VARCHAR = m.value::STRING
LEFT JOIN LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") wt
       ON TRUE
GROUP  BY c.rel_name, c.id
ORDER  BY total_members DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10.  The final step: output only the name of the single relation
WITH q1095 AS (
     SELECT TO_GEOGRAPHY("geometry") AS g
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_FEATURES f,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => f."all_tags") t
     WHERE  t.value:"key" = 'wikidata'
       AND  t.value:"value" = 'Q1095'
     LIMIT 1
),
candidate_rel AS (
     SELECT r."id",
            name_t.value:"value"::STRING AS rel_name
     FROM   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r,
            q1095,
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") name_t
     WHERE  name_t.value:"key" = 'name'
       AND  NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1
                        FROM   LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."all_tags") wt
                        WHERE  wt.value:"key" = 'wikidata')
       AND  ST_INTERSECTS( TO_GEOGRAPHY(r."geometry"), q1095.g )
),
scored AS (
     SELECT c.rel_name,
            c.id,
            COUNT(*) AS total_members
     FROM   candidate_rel c
     JOIN   GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.GEO_OPENSTREETMAP.PLANET_RELATIONS r
            ON r."id" = c."id",
            LATERAL FLATTEN(input => r."members") m
     GROUP  BY c.rel_name, c.id
)
SELECT s.rel_name  AS relation_name_with_most_features
FROM   scored s
ORDER  BY s.total_members DESC
LIMIT 1;
```

Each query is wrapped in the required Snowflake SQL syntax, enclosed column names with double‐quotes, and capped with `LIMIT 20` (except where a single record is required).
